From: NotaTV
Subject: [PATCH] drm/hdmi: announce as a set-top box, not a PC

The SPD infoframe said "Broadcom Videocore" with source type PC. LG TVs
then put the input in PC mode, which locks picture settings (peak
brightness, gamma) and renders HDR noticeably darker.
---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/display/drm_hdmi_state_helper.c
@@ -391,7 +391,7 @@
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
-	frame->sdi = HDMI_SPD_SDI_PC;
+	frame->sdi = HDMI_SPD_SDI_DSTB;
 
 	infoframe->set = true;
 
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/vc4/vc4_hdmi.c
@@ -617,7 +617,7 @@
 		max_bpc = 12;
 
 	ret = drmm_connector_hdmi_init(dev, connector,
-				       "Broadcom", "Videocore",
+				       "NotaTV", "NotaTV",
 				       &vc4_hdmi_connector_funcs,
 				       &vc4_hdmi_hdmi_connector_funcs,
 				       DRM_MODE_CONNECTOR_HDMIA,
